            "text": "We need to assign semantic categories to each translation. The categories are given with IDs and codes. We'll go through each translation and decide based on the gloss.\n\nLet's list the categories for quick reference:\n\n- animals: 9b5819ef-1242-41ed-8e7a-45c13134d764\n- body-parts: 38e2cb5d-bd60-47bb-9550-305bdeb0ac5d\n- desire-will: 203c6b6c-12ff-457a-ad38-027d988f0389\n- emotions-negative: 1fe3ca1d-f512-4575-b44c-166db2d2c6f9\n- emotions-positive: 87a29f83-bf3c-4c89-9ea8-b029a7293b38\n- family-kin: b4654cca-3e0d-4d2c-aeff-dd74385c11de\n- food-drink: a9ead29c-db30-411b-a8d5-4613bc4dc85d\n- garments: afaede05-a838-406c-9ed6-34124d9ab28d\n- house-dwelling: 5957d31c-8847-4430-8d46-ccc2f1bf982b\n- landscape: 40e4b0d2-e448-4db1-badb-13e6179b3a20\n- law-rule: 728d7077-b7c7-487a-8b1b-92bc878fcdbb\n- learning: d267380c-57f2-4b91-883c-4313e45bc1ac\n- motion-verbs: 4613ce33-b55b-467e-9ee3-9208ac4d35c8\n- naming-address: f4ace08b-cfb5-471a-ba2b-40b379f17401\n- phi-moksha: d9470869-8cf4-42d2-9725-5e5ac30a9be1\n- physical-action: d0d4ccda-12bd-4dcd-bf62-9e58b4e60b1c\n- plants-trees: 2e4f1ac5-00a5-4f69-827b-8d9475d6694b\n- professions: d45309fc-66d6-44fe-83ac-c46bbbc712e3\n- quantity-number: 6c642eb5-30b9-4639-99c2-f0d412832e3d\n- question-answer: bcf95b26-0828-4fe8-aace-17d3da8dbaea\n- rest-stillness: 3c581e75-2114-4176-a3ea-7f4e1432d2c7\n- ritual-worship: e39c6cd6-3bff-4c51-8cf3-1754d21aabed\n- senses: 9d037be1-7e98-4a51-bd28-f336f193df1d\n- sky-weather: 40c4d1a7-cf38-40d4-b80b-dfc0a4d0a9dd\n- social-relations: 600fbd9e-96ff-4ffe-a866-3ef42b3cf7c5\n- space-direction: ca789c69-c766-4b08-a643-96f1b2ddaec3\n- speech-acts: 1fda9c3b-6c20-41ea-b600-19bbffb5b627\n- thought-memory: d8df5453-0f4a-496d-afd4-115767c0bcd0\n- time-seasons: a0c5476d-68ad-474e-9081-62225c23cadd\n- tools-materials: eb16a06f-2932-4b1f-b93d-7b14f24f31be\n- travel-vehicles: 4a2c27b2-4471-4324-a0b8-9b797615cf06\n- war-conflict: 5b1c3fe3-0dd5-4144-8009-4596fb87a324\n- water: 478db819-9929-4772-af90-bf273c8f4462\n\nNow process each translation:\n\n1. id: be929355-35cc-445b-ab16-9e8ee238486b, lemma: ā, gloss: \"an interjection of reminiscence\" -> This is an interjection, not clearly fitting any category. Possibly speech-acts? But \"reminiscence\" might relate to thought-memory? However, it's an interjection, so maybe speech-acts. But careful: \"interjection\" is a speech act. So assign speech-acts? But the category is \"speech-acts: Речевые акты / Speech acts\". Yes, that fits. Also could be thought-memory? But the gloss says \"interjection of reminiscence\" - it's a speech act expressing reminiscence. So speech-acts. No other. So [speech-acts].\n\n2. id: 801a36cf-6062-4c76-8b40-ba88f5844c0d, lemma: abala, gloss: \"weak, feeble\" -> This is an adjective describing a quality. Could be emotions-negative? Not exactly. It's a state of being weak. Possibly physical-action? No. It's more like a general attribute. No clear category. Maybe none. But \"weak\" could be negative? But the category is emotions-negative, not general negative. So none.\n\n3. id: 166d4da5-d419-4417-a366-dd2fb69446fc, lemma: abda, gloss: \"a cloud, year\" -> cloud: sky-weather? Yes, cloud is weather/sky. Also year: time-seasons. So both. So [sky-weather, time-seasons].\n\n4. id: 7843dea3-354d-4f87-bfe2-a5addde1cee1, lemma: ābha, gloss: \"like, resembling\" -> This is a suffix or adjective meaning similar. Not a clear category. Possibly naming-address? No. None.\n\n5. id: 92d336fb-6fdb-43d8-bd9d-6bfc3b3cbd23, lemma: ābhā, gloss: \"splendour, beauty, appearance\" -> This is about appearance. Could be senses? \"appearance\" is visual. But also positive emotion? \"beauty\" might be positive. But the category is emotions-positive. However, \"splendour\" is more like a quality. I think it's not an emotion. Maybe no category. But \"appearance\" could be related to senses? The category \"senses\" is about sense organs, not perception. So probably none.\n\n6. id: fbae8159-b739-400f-95f4-a30b27b716d8, lemma: ābharaṇa, gloss: \"an ornament, jewel\" -> This is an ornament, so garments? The category \"garments\" includes ornaments. So [garments].\n\n7. id: 3c8dd4a8-8d52-4d22-b021-34c0de9d6bd9, lemma: abhāva, gloss: \"non-existence, absence, want\" -> This is abstract. Could be phi-moksha? \"non-existence\" is philosophical. Also \"want\" could be desire-will? But \"want\" as noun meaning lack, not desire. So maybe phi-moksha. Also \"absence\" is general. I think phi-moksha fits for non-existence. So [phi-moksha].\n\n8. id: ef1f6181-7e48-4a31-9d4d-aae75b94826d, lemma: abhaya, gloss: \"safety, security\" -> This is a state. Could be emotions-positive? Safety is positive. But also social-relations? Not exactly. Maybe none. But \"safety\" is not an emotion. So none.\n\n9. id: e14f7198-2705-423b-8e2a-4455875f7354, lemma: abhaya, gloss: \"free from fear or danger\" -> Adjective. Same as above. None.\n\n10. id: f503c6c5-761e-4947-a528-2fa50b9d997a, lemma: abheda, gloss: \"absence of distinction, identity, close union (of the body)\" -> This is abstract. Could be phi-moksha? \"identity\" and \"union\" are philosophical. Also \"body\" might relate to body-parts? But it's about union of body. Not directly. So [phi-moksha].\n\n11. id: 3e965c8e-30d4-485e-9111-2b58a82bde9e, lemma: abhi, gloss: \"to, near, towards, against\" -> This is a preposition/prefix indicating direction. So space-direction. [space-direction].\n\n12. id: be398882-8145-49d2-8992-2818a5229120, lemma: abhidhā, gloss: \"appellation, name\" -> This is about naming. So naming-address. [naming-address].\n\n13. id: 87993e39-df21-46e1-953f-c1bc1e7a1e5b, lemma: abhimāna, gloss: \"affection\" -> This is a positive emotion? Affection is positive. So emotions-positive. [emotions-positive].\n\n14. id: 7dfa125d-119d-40d8-a181-37a805fb3853, lemma: abhimāna, gloss: \"pride, haughtiness\" -> Pride can be positive or negative? Here \"haughtiness\" is negative. So emotions-negative. [emotions-negative].\n\n15. id: fbbb79