ratum\" -> Abstract. Could be phi-moksha? Philosophical concept. So [phi-moksha].\n\n44. id: 219f3f0c-aeda-4343-a4fc-ab14d7e8450b, lemma: adharma, gloss: \"an unjust act, injustice\" -> This is about law/ethics. So law-rule. Also emotions-negative? Injustice might cause negative emotion, but the word itself is not an emotion. So [law-rule].\n\n45. id: 5a3d3549-f5f3-4e9a-9919-ef670b26b107, lemma: adhas, gloss: \"below, down\" -> Space-direction. [space-direction].\n\n46. id: 03c54351-47cf-4823-930c-af653892bfc5, lemma: adhi, gloss: \"above, over, up, besides\" -> Space-direction. [space-direction].\n\n47. id: d332738d-42a9-4b55-b530-4a8ab1c6e8ac, lemma: adhika, gloss: \"surpassing, extraordinary, greater, better, higher, further, more\" -> Quantity-number? \"more\" is quantity. Also \"better\" is quality. So [quantity-number].\n\n48. id: 0a078c20-d571-4f44-af5f-2391883c2fe7, lemma: adhikāra, gloss: \"supervision, administration, office\" -> This is about governance. So law-rule. Also professions? Office is a position. So [law-rule, professions].\n\n49. id: cf383dc7-342c-40ea-a00b-e096f4fce872, lemma: adhīna, gloss: \"dependent on, subject to\" -> This is about social relations? Dependency. So social-relations. Also law-rule? Subject to authority. So [social-relations, law-rule].\n\n50. id: d6ac8a44-0533-4a39-a95c-1fc75f661c88, lemma: adhipa, gloss: \"а ruler, king\" -> This is a profession/ruler. So professions, law-rule. [professions, law-rule].\n\n51. id: 3d528c3a-dda2-47e7-ade9-f903ca8f3160, lemma: adhomukha, gloss: \"having the face downwards\" -> This is a posture. Space-direction? \"downwards\" is direction. So [space-direction].\n\n52. id: 33bf3dec-e954-4f15-a41a-a3855e8514ff, lemma: adhunā, gloss: \"at this time, now\" -> Time. So time-seasons. [time-seasons].\n\n53. id: 8599735c-4ca4-49a7-a19e-2cdee09cb45c, lemma: adhvan, gloss: \"а way, march, distance\" -> This is about travel? Way and march are travel. Also space-direction? Distance is spatial. So [travel