        "reasoning": "We are given a list of semantic categories and a batch of translations. For each translation, we need to assign one or more semantic category IDs from the provided list. The translations are English glosses of Sanskrit lemmas. We need to decide which categories the meaning of the translation belongs to.\n\nLet's go through each translation one by one.\n\n1. translation_id: \"801a36cf-6062-4c76-8b40-ba88f5844c0d\", lemma_iast: \"abala\", gloss: \"weak, feeble\". This is an adjective describing a state of being weak. It could relate to negative emotions? Not exactly. It might be a physical state? Possibly \"physical-action\" but that is for actions. There is no category for \"quality\" or \"attribute\". The closest might be \"emotions-negative\" if it's a feeling, but \"weak\" is more of a physical or general condition. Alternatively, \"rest-stillness\" might be a stretch. I think it's not clearly fitting any category. Maybe \"desire-will\" is related to will? No. I'll leave it empty.\n\n2. translation_id: \"7843dea3-354d-4f87-bfe2-a5addde1cee1\", lemma_iast: \"ābha\", gloss: \"like, resembling\". This is a comparison, akin to \"similar\". It could be related to \"naming-address\" or \"speech-acts\"? Not really. Possibly \"thought-memory\" for comparison? Or \"question-answer\"? No. It's a relational term. I think it doesn't fit any category well. Maybe \"senses\" for appearance? Not directly. I'll leave empty.\n\n3. translation_id: \"d79a8e4d-8ae0-470e-99ee-8a2b662410e0\", lemma_iast: \"acchidra\", gloss: \"free from clefts, uninterrupted, unhurt\". This describes something whole, unhurt. Possibly \"emotions-positive\" for being unhurt? Or \"rest-stillness\" for uninterrupted? Not sure. \"unhurt\" could relate to \"body-parts\" (if referring to body) but it's not specific. I think no clear category.\n\n4. translation_id: \"bee197f9-e2c9-4ce1-9391-21f226423668\", lemma_iast: \"akṣata\", gloss: \"not crushed, uninjured\". Similar to above, \"uninj