        "reasoning": "We are given a list of semantic categories and a batch of translations. For each translation, we need to assign the most appropriate semantic category IDs from the provided list. The translations are all adjectives or adverbs or nouns, etc. We need to decide based on the gloss.\n\nLet's go through each translation:\n\n1. id: 801a36cf-6062-4c76-8b40-ba88f5844c0d, lemma: abala, gloss: \"weak, feeble\"\n   This describes a quality, not really fitting any category. Possibly \"emotions-negative\"? No, it's a physical or general weakness. Not clear. Could be \"desire-will\"? No. I think it doesn't match any category well. Maybe none.\n\n2. id: 7843dea3-354d-4f87-bfe2-a5addde1cee1, lemma: ābha, gloss: \"like, resembling\"\n   This is a comparative or similarity. Could be \"naming-address\"? No. \"Thought-memory\"? Not really. Probably no category.\n\n3. id: d79a8e4d-8ae0-470e-99ee-8a2b662410e0, lemma: acchidra, gloss: \"free from clefts, uninterrupted, unhurt\"\n   This is a state of being unhurt. Could be \"rest-stillness\"? Uninterrupted might relate to continuity. But not clear. Perhaps no category.\n\n4. id: bee197f9-e2c9-4ce1-9391-21f226423668, lemma: akṣata, gloss: \"not crushed, uninjured\"\n   Similar to above. Not clearly fitting.\n\n5. id: dd0aafaf-1351-4da6-8d61-467da9f22f77, lemma: amogha, gloss: \"not vain, useful\"\n   \"Useful\" could be positive? But not a category. Maybe \"desire-will\"? No.\n\n6. id: 44165f69-551b-427a-a6ea-577c5b2b3bbe, lemma: anurūpa, gloss: \"suitable, fit\"\n   This is a quality. No clear category.\n\n7. id: 0b1d763f-0360-4767-a574-c13c050182b5, lemma: api, gloss: \"and, also, besides, very, only\"\n   This is a conjunction/adverb. Possibly \"question-answer\"? No. \"Speech-acts\"? Maybe? But it's a particle. Not sure.\n\n8. id: 12bd4e8d-2475-44d4-90fd-621d78b6733f, lemma: āpta, gloss: \"got, gained\"\n   This is a verb participle. Could be \"physical-action\"? Getting something? Or \"professions\"? No.\n\n9. id: 816e83d0-bc2c-4259-bcb1-50b771c20ad8, lemma: asādhya, gloss: \"impracticable\"\n   Negative quality. No category.\n\n10. id: 696f4ff5-5775-4aef-89cf-36b8a32ec156, lemma: atha, gloss: \"however\"\n    Conjunction. Not a category.\n\n11. id: 6d0941c1-9c0f-457a-b29f-e26c434fc9e4, lemma: atha, gloss: \"further, therefore\"\n    Again, conjunction.\n\n12. id: 63532410-0e9c-4ba7-ac48-3f5027a7acc9, lemma: atula, gloss: \"unequalled\"\n    Quality. No.\n\n13. id: c4068d7d-95ba-44f1-aefb-35cb05e5b1e9, lemma: babhru, gloss: \"brown\"\n    Color. Not a category. Possibly \"garments\"? No. \"Animals\"? No. \n\n14. id: ba740455-88f4-4ade-a615-e5c456deca93, lemma: balin, gloss: \"powerful, strong\"\n    Quality. Could be \"desire-will\"? No. \"Physical-action\"? Not directly.\n\n15. id: e204cb6d-fde1-43e9-969f-aeabbd4b6262, lemma: bhogin, gloss: \"having curves\"\n    Describes shape. Not a category.\n\n16. id: 059b75f6-74a4-4c19-ba5c-6d3bf137d12d, lemma: bhṛśa, gloss: \"adv. very\"\n    Adverb of intensity. No.\n\n17. id: fe5439d4-8ac0-443e-924b-392d98e621eb, lemma: bhṛśa, gloss: \"strong, intense, powerful\"\n    Quality. No.\n\n18. id: c726e533-981d-4026-8e45-87e4d0deaac3, lemma: bhṛtya, gloss: \"a servant, minister\"\n    This is a person. Could be \"professions\" (occupations and professions). Also \"social-relations\"? Possibly both. \"Social-relations\" includes servants? The category \"social-relations\" is about social relations, not necessarily occupations. \"Professions\" is more specific. I think \"professions\" fits well. Also \"family-kin\"? No. So assign \"professions\".\n\n19. id: 6f4e1e23-7374-41de-a06e-cfe85f7f449d, lemma: bhṛtya, gloss: \"to be nourished\"\n    This is a verb passive infinitive? \"to be nourished\" relates to food? \"Food-drink\"? Possibly. But it's about nourishment. Could be \"food-drink\" or \"physical-action\"? Not sure. \"Food-drink\" seems plausible.\n\n20. id: 2fb31a84-07ad-4f1e-92d8-207156338a05, lemma: bhrū, gloss: \"eyebrow\"\n    This is a body part. It fits \"body-parts\" clearly.\n\nSo only some translations have clear matches. Let's list them:\n\n- bhṛtya (servant) -> professions (c726e533-981d-4026-8e45-87e4d0deaac3) and maybe social-relations? But I'll stick with professions.\n- bhṛtya (to be nourished) -> food-drink? Possibly.\n- bhrū (eyebrow) -> body-parts.\n\nOthers seem to have no clear category. But we should also consider if any other could fit. For example, \"balin\" (powerful) could be \"desire-will\"? No. \"abala\" (weak) could be \"emotions-negative\"? No, it's not an emotion. So likely many are empty.\n\nWe need to return exactly one result per translation, even if empty array.\n\nLet's produce JSON.\n\nI'll assign empty for most, and for the three: servant -> professions, to be nourished -> food-drink, eyebrow -> body-parts.\n\nBut let's double-check \"to be nourished\": is it definitely food-drink? The category is \"Food and drink\". Nourishment is about food, so yes.\n\nAlso, \"bhṛtya\" as servant: could also be \"social-relations\"? But I think \"professions\" is more direct. However, \"social-relations\" might include servant as a social role. But the category \"social-relations\" says \"Социальные связи / Social relations\", which might be broader. Since we have \"professions\", I'll use that.\n\nAlso note: for \"api\" (and, also, besides, very, only) – could be \"question-answer\"? No. \"speech-acts\"? Possibly as a conjunction? But I think it's too vague.\n\nI'll go with my initial assessment.",
