        "reasoning": "We are given a list of semantic classes and a batch of translations. For each translation, we need to assign zero or more semantic class IDs from the provided list. The translations are English glosses of Sanskrit lemmas. We need to decide based on the meaning of the gloss.\n\nLet's go through each translation:\n\n1. translation_id: \"801a36cf-6062-4c76-8b40-ba88f5844c0d\", lemma_iast: \"abala\", gloss: \"weak, feeble\". This is a quality. None of the categories seem to directly fit. Possibly \"rest-stillness\"? No, weak is not rest. Or \"physical-action\"? Not really. Maybe no category. I'll check if any category matches: \"weak, feeble\" could be related to \"Negative emotions\"? No, it's a physical state. Not really. So likely empty array.\n\n2. \"d79a8e4d-8ae0-470e-99ee-8a2b662410e0\", \"acchidra\", gloss: \"free from clefts, uninterrupted, unhurt\". This is a description of wholeness. Not fitting any category. Maybe \"rest-stillness\"? Uninterrupted could be continuous, but not exactly. Probably empty.\n\n3. \"bee197f9-e2c9-4ce1-9391-21f226423668\", \"akṣata\", gloss: \"not crushed, uninjured\". Similar to above, maybe no category.\n\n4. \"dd0aafaf-1351-4da6-8d61-467da9f22f77\", \"amogha\", gloss: \"not vain, useful\". Useful could be related to \"Knowledge and learning\"? Not sure. Or \"Occupations and professions\"? No. Probably empty.\n\n5. \"44165f69-551b-427a-a6ea-577c5b2b3bbe\", \"anurūpa\", gloss: \"suitable, fit\". Again, abstract quality. Maybe \"Social relations\"? Not really. Empty.\n\n6. \"12bd4e8d-2475-44d4-90fd-621d78b6733f\", \"āpta\", gloss: \"got, gained\". This is a verb-like meaning, but the gloss is past participle. Could be \"Physical action\"? Getting/gaining is an action. But also \"Desire and will\"? Not exactly. \"Quantity and number\"? No. I think \"Physical action\" might be appropriate if we consider \"to gain\" as an action. But the gloss is \"got, gained\" which is result. However, the category is \"Physical action\". I'll assign it.\n\n7. \"816e83d0-bc2c-4259-bcb1-50b771c20ad8\", \"asādhya\", gloss: \"impracticable\". Not matching any category. Empty.\n\n8. \"63532410-0e9c-4ba7-ac48-3f5027a7acc9\", \"atula\", gloss: \"unequalled\". Abstract, no category.\n\n9. \"f6b589b9-4973-4f04-a693-666dc352f5db\", \"chidra\", gloss: \"pierced, containing holes\". This is a physical state. Could be \"Physical action\"? Not action, but state. \"Tools and materials\"? Not really. No category.\n\n10. \"cec36b0d-8d19-483f-8695-f93f88894617\", \"citraka\", gloss: \"\" (empty). No information, so empty array.\n\n11. \"6080228f-23ac-4995-9b55-342a918d25c9\", \"citta\", gloss: \"observed, intended, wished\". This is related to mind, thought, will. \"Thought and memory\" could be appropriate. Also \"Desire and will\" for \"intended, wished\". So I'll assign both d8df5453-0f4a-496d-afd4-115767c0bcd0 (thought-memory) and 203c6b6c-12ff-457a-ad38-027d988f0389 (desire-will).\n\n12. \"b30461ae-7169-4e42-b6a1-8dde2b74276f\", \"cūrṇa\", gloss: \"dust, powder, aromatic powder\". This is a substance. Could be \"Tools and materials\"? Dust is material. Also \"Food and drink\"? Not exactly, aromatic powder might be used in food. But \"Plants and trees\"? No. I think \"Tools and materials\" is closest. Also maybe \"Landscape and terrain\"? Dust is part of landscape? Not really. I'll assign \"Tools and materials\".\n\n13. \"04e32f13-296e-4a9d-87e2-53c8ad429383\", \"cūrṇa\", gloss: \"minute\". This is an adjective meaning small. \"Quantity and number\"? Possibly. But \"minute\" as in very small, not a number. Could be \"Space and direction\"? No. I think no category.\n\n14. \"3a35d2fa-7e8a-42a7-aa19-cb4c417c9d20\", \"cūrṇay\", gloss: \"to grind, pulverize, crush, bruise\". This is a physical action. So assign \"Physical action\".\n\n15. \"3950050c-2bf9-4592-9270-efd78ecc8e22\", \"cyavana\", gloss: \"falling, moving, motion, change, loss\". This is clearly about motion. Assign \"Motion verbs\" (since the root is cyu, a verb of motion) and also \"Rest and stillness\"? No, it's the opposite. So assign \"Motion verbs\".\n\n16. \"a4f4ede7-0b73-4890-ad20-c73a8f53a963\", \"cyu\", gloss: \"to move to and fro, fall down, sink, be deprived of\". Again motion verbs. Assign \"Motion verbs\".\n\n17. \"ff6cb01e-d6cd-400f-8f91-9606e22b2371\", \"da\", gloss: \"giving, producing\". This is a physical action (giving) and also possibly \"Social relations\" (giving as exchange). But the root is \"da\" meaning to give. I think \"Physical action\" is appropriate.\n\n18. \"e4e86b71-4719-45e8-866c-926d8231dbe4\", \"dā\", gloss: \"permit, allow\". This is a speech act? \"Permit\" is a kind of speech act. Also \"Law and governance\"? Possibly. But more directly \"Speech acts\". Also \"Social relations\"? Not sure. I'll assign \"Speech acts\".\n\n19. \"a9f6ef23-6e9d-4888-9ec0-d08527daeff1\", \"dā\", gloss: \"to pay (as debt)\". This is a physical action (giving money) and also \"Law and governance\" (debt, payment). Also \"Social relations\"? Possibly. I'll assign \"Physical action\" and \"Law and governance\".\n\n20. \"e446ccbe-350f-4d92-b58c-5013a2af6fc9\", \"dā\", gloss: \"give in marriage\". This is a social act, related to family and social relations. \"Family and relatives\" is appropriate. Also \"Social relations\". And \"Ritual and worship\"? Marriage is a ritual. But the category is \"Ritual and worship\". So assign \"Family and relatives\", \"Social relations\", and \"Ritual and worship\".\n\nNow, let's compile the results.\n\nMake sure to use the correct IDs.",
