But it's a name. Also \"ritual-worship\"? ṛṣi are associated with rituals. \"Learning\"? Possibly. \"Philosophy and liberation\"? Maybe. I think \"ritual-worship\" is appropriate because ṛṣi are involved in Vedic rituals. Also \"naming-address\" for the name itself. I'll assign both \"naming-address\" and \"ritual-worship\".\n\n12. id: 8adf0ff0-fb06-4ea6-a730-40b2c206984e, lemma: aṅguli, gloss: \"a finger, toe\". Body parts, so \"body-parts\".\n\n13. id: 1c47e2b8-59ce-4d9c-97ce-c927e01fefcf, lemma: anila, gloss: \"wind\". Wind is weather, so \"sky-weather\". Also \"landscape\"? No. So assign \"sky-weather\".\n\n14. id: 5b63c3c7-64e0-4b93-8c0e-f2240b7e03a4, lemma: aṇiman, gloss: \"fineness, fine particle, minuteness\". This is abstract. Could be \"quantity-number\"? Fineness is not quantity. \"Space-direction\"? No. \"Thought-memory\"? No. I think no category fits. Leave empty.\n\n15. id: 3485aa18-3cbe-40a2-83f3-cd67e8ff3009, lemma: añj, gloss: \"to smear, anoint, decorate, make clear\". This is a verb. \"Physical action\" for smearing, anointing. Also \"ritual-worship\" because anointing can be part of rituals. \"Garments\"? Decorate could be related to ornaments. But the verb is action. I'll assign \"physical-action\" and possibly \"ritual-worship\". Also \"tools-materials\"? No. So assign \"physical-action\" and \"ritual-worship\".\n\n16. id: 9dad8462-bc29-4567-9465-64c9033330ac, lemma: añjali, gloss: \"the two hollowed palms put together, salutation, a measure\". This is a gesture, often used in greeting or worship. So \"ritual-worship\" for salutation. Also \"body-parts\" for palms? But it's a specific gesture. \"Naming-address\"? No. \"Speech-acts\"? Salutation is a speech act? But it's a physical gesture. I think \"ritual-worship\" is most appropriate. Also \"physical-action\"? Possibly. But I'll go with \"ritual-worship\".\n\n17. id: c9f21bfb-09ee-4a17-ac7f-26c5892c3c5a, lemma: añjana, gloss: \"smearing, anointing, ointment, antimony\". This is a substance used for anointing. Could be \"tools-materials\" for ointment. Also \"ritual-worship\" for anointing. \"Garments\"? No. \"Body-parts\"? No. So assign \"tools-materials\" and \"ritual-worship\".\n\n18. id: 1a032cce-fb95-461a-b93a-5db01daaa7e7, lemma: aṅka, gloss: \"а hook, bend, lap, flank\". \"Hook\" is a tool, so \"tools-materials\". \"Bend\" could be shape. \"Lap, flank\" are body parts. So multiple: \"tools-materials\" for hook, \"body-parts\" for lap/flank. Also \"physical-action\"? No. So assign \"tools-materials\" and \"body-parts\".\n\n19. id: a2eecbc1-2b13-4079-8efc-9514cfb40a89, lemma: aṅkura, gloss: \"a shoot, sprout -vant poss.\" This is a plant part, so \"plants-trees\". Also \"food-drink\"? Sprouts can be food. But primarily plant. So assign \"plants-trees\".\n\n20. id: c4273ace-b775-4550-b0cd-46283e7de6ef, lemma: aṅkuśa, gloss: \"a hook, goad (esp. of an elephant-driver)\". This is a tool, so \"tools-materials\". Also \"animals\"? Related to elephants. But the goad itself is a tool. So assign \"tools-materials\".\n\nNow, we need to output JSON with translation_id and semantic_class_ids. For each translation, we list the IDs of the categories we assigned.\n\nLet's map the category IDs:\n\n- animals: 9b5819ef-1242-41ed-8e7a-45c13134d764\n- body-parts: 38e2cb5d-bd60-47bb-9550-305bdeb0ac5d\n- desire-will: 203c6b6c-12ff-457a-ad38-027d988f0389\n- emotions-negative: 1fe3ca1d-f512-4575-b44c-166db2d2c6f9\n- emotions-positive: 87a29f83-bf3c-4c89-9ea8-b029a7293b38\n- family-kin: b4654cca-3e0d-4d2c-aeff-dd74385c11de\n- food-drink: a9ead29c-db30-411b-a8d5-4613bc4dc85d\n- garments: afaede05-a838-406c-9ed6-34124d9ab28d\n- house-dwelling: 5957d31c-8847-4430-8d46-ccc2f1bf982b\n- landscape: 40e4b0d2-e448-4db1-badb-13e6179b3a20\n- law-rule: 728d7077-b7c7-487a-8b1b-92bc878fcdbb\n- learning: d267380c-57f2-4b91-883c-4313e45bc1ac\n- motion-verbs: 4613ce33-b55b-467e-9ee3-9208ac4d35c8\n- naming-address: f4ace08b-cfb5-471a-ba2b-40b379f17401\n- phi-moksha: d9470869-8cf4-42d2-9725-