ion_id: \"9ac9c473-0ba8-4f01-84bb-16424c9ef3f0\", lemma: \"apaharaṇa\", gloss: \"taking away, carrying off, annihilation\". This is a physical action? \"taking away\" is physical action. Also \"annihilation\" could be war-conflict. I'll assign \"physical-action\" and \"war-conflict\".\n\n6. translation_id: \"ce1c5ff4-0194-4cec-bcc8-b9200aacdfe4\", lemma: \"apakarṣaṇa\", gloss: \"taking away, drawing down, undressing\". This is physical action. \"undressing\" relates to garments? But it's the action of removing garments. I'll assign \"physical-action\" and possibly \"garments\" for undressing? But \"garments\" is about clothing items, not actions. I'll stick with \"physical-action\".\n\n7. translation_id: \"05e83615-e2e2-42ff-ba36-8bf2804047f5\", lemma: \"apāna\", gloss: \"breathing out\". This is a bodily function. Could be \"body-parts\"? No, it's an action. \"physical-action\"? Breathing is a physical action. Also \"senses\"? No. I'll assign \"physical-action\".\n\n8. translation_id: \"db65e8ae-cbfe-4598-80f0-d533f2805a5c\", lemma: \"āpaṇa\", gloss: \"a market\". This is a place. Could be \"house-dwelling\"? No, market is a commercial place. \"professions\"? Not directly. \"social-relations\"? Market is a social place. I think \"house-dwelling\" is about houses, not markets. \"landscape\"? No. \"travel-vehicles\"? No. I'll assign \"social-relations\" because market involves social interaction. Also possibly \"professions\" if we consider market as a place of trade? But the category is \"occupations and professions\", not places. I'll go with \"social-relations\".\n\n9. translation_id: \"f507ac6c-2d1e-4b89-afb8-351f469395f4\", lemma: \"apāṅga\", gloss: \"the outer corner of the eye\". This is a body part. So \"body-parts\". Also \"senses\" because eye is a sense organ. I'll assign both \"body-parts\" and \"senses\".\n\n10. translation_id: \"4962a09d-3d60-49ab-952f-afc98d28c20f\", lemma: \"aparādha\", gloss: \"sin, fault, transgression\". This relates to law/rule? Sin is religious, but also social. \"law-rule\" for transgression? \"emotions-negative\"? Possibly. \"ritual-worship\"? Sin is often religious. I'll assign \"law-rule\" and \"ritual-worship\". Also \"emotions-negative\"? Not directly an emotion. I'll stick with \"law-rule\" and \"ritual-worship\".\n\n11. translation_id: \"0a68a591-6d6c-445b-8c52-884d99640646\", lemma: \"aparapakṣa\", gloss: \"the latter half of the month\". This is time-related. So \"time-seasons\".\n\n12. translation_id: \"2f4a2c48-f8d6-4c6c-84e5-49d4acfbe4cb\", lemma: \"apatya\", gloss: \"offspring, child, а young one\". This is family/kin. So \"family-kin\".\n\n13. translation_id: \"4d2033aa-8739-4b3a-b1d4-4eb0894dd091\", lemma: \"apavāda\", gloss: \"refutation, blame, speaking ill of\". This is speech acts. \"speech-acts\". Also \"emotions-negative\"? Blame is negative. I'll assign \"speech-acts\" and \"emotions-negative\".\n\n14. translation_id: \"6172d4f6-e206-4e3f-948e-74a7075578bb\", lemma: \"apavarga\", gloss: \"end, final delivery, redemption\". This could be philosophy/liberation (moksha). \"phi-moksha\" fits redemption. Also \"time-seasons\"? End could be time. But \"redemption\" is more philosophical. I'll assign \"phi-moksha\".\n\n15. translation_id: \"aa8af82d-3dff-4a3b-9acd-a719d14121c5\", lemma: \"apāya\", gloss: \"going away, end, death\". This could be motion verbs? \"going away\" is motion. \"end\" and \"death\" are not motion. \"death\" could be \"emotions-negative\"? Not exactly. \"phi-moksha\"? Death is related to liberation? Possibly. I'll assign \"motion-verbs\" for \"going away\", and \"phi-moksha\" for death? But \"phi-moksha\" is about philosophy and liberation, not death per se. I'll assign \"motion-verbs\" and maybe \"emotions-negative\"? I think \"death\" is not an emotion. I'll go with \"motion-verbs\" only.\n\n16. translation_id: \"90374b26-3e78-4530-986b-9b469cb70c1b\", lemma: \"apekṣā\", gloss: \"regard to, expectation\". This is thought/memory? Expectation is a mental state. \"thought-memory\" fits. Also \"desire-will\"? Expectation involves desire. I'll assign \"thought-memory\" and \"desire-will\".\n\n17. translation_id: \"220f44ec-4668-4ec2-ac2e-82fb041a1d24\", lemma: \"api\", gloss: \"and, also, besides, very, only\". This is a conjunction/adverb. No clear category. Possibly \"question-answer\"? No. \"speech-acts\"? No. I'll leave empty.\n\n18. translation_id: \"85f689d2-9cd4-4142-bb70-d005c20aec93\", lemma: \"āpi\", gloss: \"a friend, fellow\". This is social relations. \"social-relations\". Also \"family-kin\"? Friend is not necessarily kin. I'll assign \"social-relations\".\n\n19. translation_id: \"d705159b-7f82-415a-a034-c854810ae3ae\", lemma: \"apsaras\", gloss: \"impudent (?), a nymph\". A nymph is a mythological being. Could be \"ritual-worship\"? Nymphs are often in mythology. Also \"animals\"? No. \"landscape\"? No. I think \"ritual-worship\" might fit because they are divine beings. Also \"emotions-positive\"? Not sure. I'll assign \"ritual-worship\".\n\n20. translation_id: \"0a890a94-2896-42ac-bbc2-77ba5796dd01\", lemma: \"āpti\", gloss: \"obtaining, gain\". This could be \"desire-will\"? Obtaining is related to desire. Also \"physical-action\"? Not necessarily. \"social-relations\"? Gain could be social. I'll assign \"desire-will\".\n\nNow, we need to output JSON with the results. Each result should have translation_id and semantic_class_ids (array of IDs). If no category, empty array.\n\nLet's compile the IDs:\n\n1. 8edf867e-0223-4bd7-abab-0675e8385d84: [] (empty)\n2. 024e3573-8f71-44e9-8a79-b17505d5c321: []\n3. f449e27c-09f5-4a5f-88a7-e2048594f5ef: [\"600fbd9e-96ff-4ffe-a866-3ef42b3cf7c5\", \"87a29f83-bf3c-4c89-9ea8-b029a7293b38\"] (social-relations, emotions-positive)\n4. e04cd1f2-9601-42cd-b717-77c8887f4788: [\"1fe3ca1d-f512-4575-b44c-166db2d2c6f9\"] (emotions-negative)\n5. 9ac9c473-0ba8-4f01-84bb-16424c9ef3f0: [\"d0d4ccda-12bd-4dcd-bf62-9e58b4e60b1c\", \"5b1c3fe3-0dd5-4144-8009-4596fb87a324\"] (physical-a