        "reasoning": "We are given a list of semantic categories and a batch of translations. For each translation, we need to assign zero or more semantic class IDs from the provided list. The categories are specific leaf categories. We need to map each translation to the most appropriate category based on its gloss.\n\nLet's go through each translation one by one.\n\n1. translation_id: \"8edf867e-0223-4bd7-abab-0675e8385d84\", lemma_iast: \"ākāra\", gloss: \"form, stature, appearance\". This seems to relate to shape or appearance. Could be \"senses\" (senses) or \"body-parts\"? But \"form\" is more abstract. Possibly \"space-direction\"? Not exactly. \"senses\" is about sense organs, not appearance. \"body-parts\" is about body parts. \"form\" might be more general. There is no category for \"shape\" or \"appearance\". Perhaps \"naming-address\"? No. I think it doesn't fit well into any category. Maybe \"senses\" because appearance is perceived by sight? But \"senses\" category is \"Органы чувств / Senses\" which is about sense organs, not the quality. I'll leave it empty.\n\n2. translation_id: \"024e3573-8f71-44e9-8a79-b17505d5c321\", lemma_iast: \"anyathā\", gloss: \"otherwise\". This is an adverb. Could be \"question-answer\"? No. \"space-direction\"? Not really. \"time-seasons\"? No. It's a manner adverb. No category fits. Empty.\n\n3. translation_id: \"220f44ec-4668-4ec2-ac2e-82fb041a1d24\", lemma_iast: \"api\", gloss: \"and, also, besides, very, only\". This is a conjunction/particle. No category fits. Empty.\n\n4. translation_id: \"aa316b7e-0cc4-4682-8781-7605d36bc931\", lemma_iast: \"apūpa\", gloss: \"cake\". This is a food item. Category \"food-drink\" (id: a9ead29c-db30-411b-a8d5-4613bc4dc85d) fits.\n\n5. translation_id: \"b813dba2-9ba1-495c-b597-c145ea82de19\", lemma_iast: \"ara\", gloss: \"the spoke of a wheel\". This is a part of a vehicle. Category \"travel-vehicles\" (id: 4a2c27b2-4471-4324-a0b8-9b797615cf06) might fit, but spoke is a part of a whee